0..82 Comment "// `Path.step(p, q)` moves `p` along `q` in `y. Path(A, a, y)`, and that transport"
83..160 Comment "// appends on its first word whatever `q` is: the empty word is the unit, and"
161..226 Comment "// a letter stays first. Two definitions whose composites are one"
227..288 Comment "// transport, stuck on its two parameters, name one path. The"
289..363 Comment "// composite and its unit laws are the HoTT book\'s Lemmas 2.1.2 and 2.1.4."
364..366 Comment "//"
367..411 Comment "// - see: #422 — `leftUnit`, `letterFirst`"
412..465 Comment "// - see: #440 — `sameComposite`, `sameAfterLetter`"
